Time Complexity vs Space Complexity: Measuring Execution time vs. 
additional memory usage as input size (n) grows

Asymptotic Growth Rates: O(1) Constant Time, O(logn) Logarithmic Time
O(n) Linear Time, O(nlogn) Linearithmic time (Mergesort, Quicksort)
O(n^2) Quadratic time (bubble sort, etc)

Best, Average, and Worst-Case Analysis: Big-O- Upper Bound (worst case)
Big-Omega- Lower bound (best case)
Counting Operations: Dropping constants and keeping dominating terms
(Higher Order Variables)

Array Core Operation: Access/Read- BC O(1), WC O(1), Complexity O(1)
Update- BC O(1), O(1), Complexity O(1)
Linear Search- BC O(1), WC O(n), Complexity O(1)

Recursion vs Iteration: Trade-offs between readability/elegance and 
memory overhead (stack frame allocation)

Sorting Algorithms: BubbleSort- BC O(n), WC O(n^2) Complexity O(1)
SelectionSort- BC O(n^2), WC O(n^2), Complexity O(1)
InsertionSort- BC O(n), WC O(n^2), Complexity O(1)
MergeSort- BC O(nlogn), WC O(nlogn), Complexity O(n)
QuickSort- BC O(nlogn), WC O(N^2), Complexity O(logn)(stack)

